      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Dry runs can write through preserved symlinks",
      "description": "`copyInstallPaths` preserves symlinks with `verbatimSymlinks: true`. If an install path in the project is an absolute symlink, the sandbox copy can still point to the original target. The installer then writes through that link during the dry run, modifying files outside the sandbox despite the guarantee that nothing is written. Ensure the sandbox contains no links that resolve to the real project or external paths before running the installer.",
